WEBVTT

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:13.180
Romeo's Blue Skies

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:12.820
"To the Sky..."

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:17.880
<i>Overlooking the rows of houses and stores</i>

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:22.290
<i>from the highest vantage,</i>

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:27.400
<i>Such things as tears and sadness</i>

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:31.540
<i>will quickly vanish</i>

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:37.100
<i>The birds, wind, and sunshine...</i>

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:41.290
<i>...all are your friends</i>

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:46.360
<i>I'll carry this dream farther than far</i>

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:51.450
<i>...no matter the distance...</i>

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:58.210
<i>I long to fly freely</i>

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:02.490
<i>through the blue sky in my heart...</i>

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:05.420
<i>The far distant blue sky</i>

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:12.870
<i>It flows into tomorrow</i>

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:25.180
Takara Fansubs

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:31.920
<i>Romeo saved the lives of Rossi and all the others.</i>

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:37.210
<i>His bravery finally brought his innocence to light.</i>

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:42.280
<i>Freed and absolved of guilt, he hurried home,</i>

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:46.310
<i>...where Angeletta had been longing for his return.</i>

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:54.980
Episode 15:

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:54.980
Strike a Light!
The Oath of the Eleven

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:05.000
<i>Rossi has now become Romeo's unwavering ally.</i>

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:17.760
<i>Romeo's room ended up looking nothing like before.</i>

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.360
And... even a bed, too?

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:26.270
Yeah. He built it for me.

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:28.890
It's bigger than a king's bed!

00:02:31.910 --> 00:02:33.810
And he said it's all right to keep Piccolo, too.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:36.120
Congratulations, Piccolo!

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:43.440
Piccolo can get his own food.
He won't cause anybody any bother.

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:45.380
And there's one more thing!
- Eh?

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:48.380
My boss gave me today off.

00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:52.760
A-ha! You're going to do some exploring,
to see if you can find Alfredo, right?

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:58.160
How did you know?
- You're always talking about him, after all...

00:02:58.250 --> 00:02:58.890
Eh?!

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:04.120
I've never met him, but I feel like I know everything about him.

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:08.060
The last time we saw each other,

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:12.010
...was the day we swore eternal friendship.

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:16.990
We'll always be together!

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:18.970
No matter how far apart they separate us!

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:25.080
No matter how far apart!

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:31.820
Dante was telling me...
He heard of a boy named Alfredo,

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:34.290
...near a street called "Ceruba Ioko".

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:36.520
I'm going to find him no matter what.

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:40.790
Boss! Ma'am!

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:43.040
I'm leaving for a bit!

00:03:43.310 --> 00:03:45.000
Sure, go on ahead!

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:50.490
Today it's just you and I to keep each other company, Piccolo!

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:53.780
Day off?

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:56.380
Just who do you think you are?

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:58.890
What gives you the right to be so indulgent?

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:01.200
We've never once before done anything of the...

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:04.660
Don't you EVER say that kind of thing in this house again!

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:19.810
I've always wanted to say that.

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:22.500
Well, then... I think I'll go out and throw back a few drinks tonight!

00:04:40.770 --> 00:04:41.850
Maybe that's it.

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:49.980
Uh, pardon me, is this Ceruba loko street?
- Yes, it is.

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:54.480
Would you know a boy named Alfredo? He's a chimney sweep.

00:04:54.990 --> 00:04:57.060
He's a slight bit taller than me...

00:04:57.540 --> 00:04:58.580
Nope...

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:04.990
I know him.

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:07.790
He's over there.

00:05:14.890 --> 00:05:15.950
Thank you.

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:31.000
Alfredo?

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:34.110
It's me.

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:35.100
It's Romeo.

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:40.350
Mom... no more chimneys...
I want to go home...

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:57.280
For Chrissake... Ohh!
I can't stand sleepless nights!

00:05:57.690 --> 00:06:01.530
Are you a chimney sweep, too?
- Who are you?

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:04.950
My name's Romeo! Do you know a boy named Alfredo?

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:07.920
Are you a friend of Alfredo's?

00:06:08.540 --> 00:06:11.290
Eh? A friend of Alfredo's?

00:06:12.110 --> 00:06:15.550
So you know him?
- Of course I do!

00:06:15.990 --> 00:06:21.170
There's not a sweep in the area who doesn't owe him one!

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:25.090
Even just last night he brought us food to eat!

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:28.810
We were starved after having slaved through the night,

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:31.620
...then he comes with a potato for us THIS BIG, and corn THIS big...!

00:06:31.790 --> 00:06:33.710
Then... where is Alfredo?

00:06:33.970 --> 00:06:35.560
Oh, it was delicious!

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:38.710
A potato THIS BIG...
and corn THIS big...!!

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:41.340
Yes, okay, but where...
- Oh yeah!

00:06:41.780 --> 00:06:44.000
Augusto might know.

00:06:44.310 --> 00:06:45.280
Augusto?

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:50.040
Yeah. He said he'd been helped out of a pinch once by him.

00:06:57.160 --> 00:07:00.690
Please tell me what you remember about the time you met Alfredo.

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:06.290
He arrived right in the nick of time, Y'see, the Wolf Pack jumped me.

00:07:06.910 --> 00:07:08.800
The Wolf Pack?
- Yeah.

00:07:10.410 --> 00:07:12.750
Those jerks, they came at me in a group.

00:07:22.660 --> 00:07:24.650
Just when I thought they were going to whack me...

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:25.550
Stop!

00:07:26.240 --> 00:07:27.100
Who's there?!

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:37.040
And I had enough time to make a break for it.

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:42.060
So... it was Alfredo, was it?

00:07:42.570 --> 00:07:46.100
Right. He stashed me in the San Babila Church that time.

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:48.850
San Babila Church...?

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:53.100
He really saved my butt.
It's all thanks to him.

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:57.690
Then, do you know where he is now, Augusto?

00:07:57.950 --> 00:08:01.440
No, I don't... I'd like to know where he is myself...

00:08:09.860 --> 00:08:12.350
<i>Where are you, Alfredo?</i>

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:14.260
Stop it! Stop it!

00:08:15.210 --> 00:08:17.590
These groceries are for my boss!

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:20.350
Who cares!
That's not our problem!

00:08:20.830 --> 00:08:22.620
Why are you doing this to me...!?

00:08:23.740 --> 00:08:25.240
We can't stand ya, that's why!

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:28.970
You chimney sweeps are all outsiders, from far away, that's why!

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:32.050
Bingo!
Tachioni, the one and only!

00:08:35.010 --> 00:08:36.660
Give it here!
- No!

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:38.660
Who threw that!

00:08:42.150 --> 00:08:44.330
Romeo!
- You bastard!

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:47.020
Dammit!

00:08:47.770 --> 00:08:49.000
Hey, you! Run!

00:08:49.950 --> 00:08:50.410
Get him!

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:52.620
Thanks...!

00:08:58.770 --> 00:08:59.650
Sorry!

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:00.640
Move!

00:09:03.170 --> 00:09:04.190
Yipes!

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:14.920
Where is he? That bastard!

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:15.960
Over there!

00:09:34.280 --> 00:09:35.250
That was close.

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:47.630
The Lord protects his congregation here at San Babila Church!

00:09:49.240 --> 00:09:50.900
San Babila Church...!

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:28.480
Alfredo...

00:10:43.570 --> 00:10:44.320
Romeo...

00:10:45.690 --> 00:10:46.550
Alfredo...

00:10:52.720 --> 00:10:53.870
Alfredo!

00:10:56.140 --> 00:10:58.870
I looked for you, Alfredo!
- I looked for you, too.

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:04.380
We've finally found each other again!

00:11:06.540 --> 00:11:08.240
And we'll be together from now on.

00:11:09.250 --> 00:11:10.090
We'll be together!

00:11:29.970 --> 00:11:33.480
Eh?! So...
So Antonio and Michaelo are still alive, too?

00:11:34.030 --> 00:11:34.510
Yeah.

00:11:35.150 --> 00:11:36.560
They're both doing great.

00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:56.780
Then we WEREN'T the only two to survive! What a relief!

00:11:57.830 --> 00:12:01.620
I'm glad to hear that Dante was okay, too.

00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:02.480
Yeah.

00:12:04.070 --> 00:12:07.400
But the Wolf Pack, acting big over on this side of town, too...

00:12:07.470 --> 00:12:08.370
...I never expected to hear that.

00:12:09.140 --> 00:12:12.890
Yeah. As soon as they see any of us, they start a fight.

00:12:14.030 --> 00:12:16.830
Damn it! Can't we do something about them...?

00:12:17.490 --> 00:12:20.120
<i>Alfredo felt the same way exactly.</i>

00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:23.970
<i>Affected by his friend Romeo's simple honesty,</i>

00:12:24.460 --> 00:12:27.680
<i>...Alfredo suddenly felt new courage filling his heart.</i>

00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:34.330
Romeo... there IS one way we could stand up to the Wolf Pack.

00:12:36.450 --> 00:12:37.790
I've been thinking it over for a while now.

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:40.900
Now that you're here, well, maybe THIS is the time to try!

00:12:41.030 --> 00:12:41.850
What is it?

00:12:42.930 --> 00:12:44.850
We'll get our friends together!

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:46.590
Our friends?

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:52.430
We'll form an alliance from all the chimney sweeps we know,

00:12:52.870 --> 00:12:55.520
...that way we can help each other and combine our courage together.

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:56.440
Our courage...?

00:12:58.270 --> 00:13:00.540
I get it! With all of us together in a group,

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:03.580
...the Wolf Pack won't be able to lay a paw on us!

00:13:06.650 --> 00:13:08.100
Here's a map.

00:13:10.370 --> 00:13:11.630
What are these marks for?

00:13:12.800 --> 00:13:16.300
Chimney sweeps live in those locations.
- Eh?

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:18.200
Antonio lives here.

00:13:18.640 --> 00:13:19.670
Michaelo's here.

00:13:20.690 --> 00:13:24.720
And I haven't met him yet, but I hear that I'll be able to count on Baltonio.

00:13:25.100 --> 00:13:26.110
Benali's here.

00:13:26.640 --> 00:13:27.810
And Enrico's here.

00:13:29.610 --> 00:13:31.970
Let's get everyone together!
We'll get into contact with each guy.

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:32.680
Yeah!

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:37.440
This Friday will be our first secret meeting.

00:13:56.550 --> 00:13:59.220
Romeo! Romeo! Romeo!

00:13:59.280 --> 00:14:01.730
I heard from Alfredo that you were still alive!

00:14:01.880 --> 00:14:05.390
Michaelo, can you sneak away for a while on Friday?

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:07.770
We're getting everyone together.

00:14:10.130 --> 00:14:12.130
Huh? Secret meeting?

00:14:14.430 --> 00:14:17.200
That sounds keen!
Peachy keen!

00:14:17.510 --> 00:14:18.940
So we just have to get our friends to come!

00:14:19.300 --> 00:14:21.190
...to this... this "Lions" thing?

00:14:21.520 --> 00:14:22.360
"Alliance"!

00:14:22.470 --> 00:14:25.160
Leave it to me! I'll fish up a hundred!

00:14:25.580 --> 00:14:28.070
Make that two-hundred! Just watch!

00:14:30.650 --> 00:14:33.650
Say what? All of us get together and trounce the Wolf Pack?!

00:14:33.910 --> 00:14:35.920
Alfredo's putting out a call to join together.

00:14:36.710 --> 00:14:37.680
Is that true?!

00:14:37.830 --> 00:14:41.470
Yeah... This guy Romeo is running around telling everybody.

00:14:43.260 --> 00:14:44.600
This Friday night?!

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:46.450
Yeah! Don't be late!

00:14:47.090 --> 00:14:48.630
Antonio...!

00:14:49.560 --> 00:14:54.080
Be careful!
What's wrong with you?

00:14:54.140 --> 00:14:58.770
Get this! Alfredo and Romeo are up to something big!

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:04.020
...Enrico ...and Benavilo, accounted for.

00:15:04.680 --> 00:15:07.570
All right! Tomorrow's the big day!

00:15:15.130 --> 00:15:19.140
<i>And then, it was finally Friday night...</i>

00:16:24.140 --> 00:16:25.490
Everyone here?

00:16:25.640 --> 00:16:26.920
Still waiting on Alfredo.

00:16:29.230 --> 00:16:30.710
I wonder what's wrong?

00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:33.790
You don't think... that his boss got wind of it?

00:16:34.240 --> 00:16:36.570
Over there!
It's Alfredo!

00:16:41.020 --> 00:16:42.660
Over here, everyone!

00:16:53.320 --> 00:16:55.330
Where are they going?
- Dunno.

00:16:55.570 --> 00:16:57.710
But I'd follow them anywhere.

00:17:00.020 --> 00:17:01.320
All right... in here!

00:17:22.420 --> 00:17:24.400
What a creepy place!

00:17:24.820 --> 00:17:26.540
Now things are really starting to get interesting!

00:17:29.050 --> 00:17:29.630
What is it?!

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:33.110
Oh, just a rat...

00:17:34.060 --> 00:17:36.500
Don't go yelling your head off on account of a measely rat, will you?

00:17:36.790 --> 00:17:37.980
S... Sorry...

00:17:47.350 --> 00:17:48.710
Come on! In here!

00:18:04.450 --> 00:18:11.400
While Napoleon occupied Milan, the resistance was hiding here.

00:18:12.080 --> 00:18:13.820
Amazing!
- This is perfect.

00:18:14.040 --> 00:18:15.760
Nobody will find us here, that's for sure!
- Magnifico!

00:18:15.870 --> 00:18:17.500
Fantastico!
- We've done it!

00:18:19.180 --> 00:18:22.150
This will be our secret base from now on.

00:18:22.770 --> 00:18:24.750
Hey, let's choose a leader!

00:18:24.860 --> 00:18:26.140
Yes, let's.

00:18:36.990 --> 00:18:39.810
It looks like everybody's made the same decision, Alfredo.

00:18:40.360 --> 00:18:40.910
Eh?

00:18:43.180 --> 00:18:46.110
Alfredo's the leader!
Anybody who disagrees with that?

00:18:46.420 --> 00:18:48.320
No way!
- I second that!

00:18:48.930 --> 00:18:50.700
It's gotta be Alfredo!

00:18:57.530 --> 00:18:58.410
Alfredo...

00:19:02.400 --> 00:19:04.670
Thank you, everybody.

00:19:07.730 --> 00:19:11.260
We'll now begin the inauguration ceremony!
- Yeah!

00:19:14.790 --> 00:19:17.430
Yo, Alfredo!
Your face is all black!

00:19:17.830 --> 00:19:21.020
So is yours, Dante, whenever you're "working"!

00:19:21.090 --> 00:19:22.680
Yours is blacker!

00:19:22.960 --> 00:19:24.180
Everybody's is black!

00:19:27.220 --> 00:19:31.780
Who cares if they're all black?
It's proof of our hard work!

00:19:32.050 --> 00:19:33.080
Yeah!

00:19:33.390 --> 00:19:34.430
Yeah!

00:19:45.840 --> 00:19:51.090
That's it, then! Let's call ourselves the "Black Brothers"!

00:19:51.620 --> 00:19:52.960
"Black Brothers"...?

00:19:53.540 --> 00:19:55.830
Because we're all brothers here!

00:19:55.890 --> 00:19:56.930
The Black Brothers...

00:19:57.220 --> 00:19:59.200
That's what we fellows will be known as?

00:19:59.400 --> 00:20:01.140
Sounds good!
- Excellent!

00:20:01.910 --> 00:20:02.420
Yeah.

00:20:03.230 --> 00:20:04.930
The Black Brothers will help each other out.

00:20:05.500 --> 00:20:10.240
If one suffers, we all suffer; if one is happy, then we're all happy!

00:20:10.680 --> 00:20:14.740
We can overcome any hardship with our strength pooled!

00:20:16.550 --> 00:20:19.940
Now! Let us share the flames of courage!

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:30.020
We'll help each other out no matter what.

00:20:30.260 --> 00:20:31.160
...no matter what!

00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:35.700
We'll stick together!
- We'll stick together!

00:20:37.420 --> 00:20:39.010
I'm scared of no-one, now!

00:20:39.600 --> 00:20:41.320
I feel a lot braver already!

00:20:41.740 --> 00:20:42.360
Me, too!

00:20:53.600 --> 00:20:56.620
Let us make an oath... by the flames of courage!

00:20:56.970 --> 00:20:58.560
...By the flames of courage!

00:21:01.670 --> 00:21:07.130
We swear from this day forth to fight bravely for our fellow Black Brothers!

00:21:07.270 --> 00:21:08.940
We swear!

00:21:09.910 --> 00:21:13.480
We swear to follow our leader in all circumstances!

00:21:13.810 --> 00:21:14.650
We swear!

00:21:15.270 --> 00:21:19.390
We swear not to reveal our secret hideout to anyone!

00:21:19.630 --> 00:21:20.450
We swear!

00:21:21.610 --> 00:21:24.770
And we swear to help each other out at all times!

00:21:25.160 --> 00:21:25.910
We swear!

00:21:28.710 --> 00:21:30.980
Good. We are now a fraternity!

00:21:31.510 --> 00:21:32.700
Fraternity!

00:21:55.250 --> 00:22:00.450
<i>Alfredo is only a year older than me, but he's a splendid leader for us.</i>

00:22:01.030 --> 00:22:03.670
<i>Comparing him with me, I seem like a mere child!</i>

00:22:04.290 --> 00:22:07.620
<i>All right then! I'm going to get closer to him!</i>

00:22:08.370 --> 00:22:11.520
See you then!

00:22:08.370 --> 00:22:11.520
<i>Alfredo is My Rival!</i>

00:22:08.370 --> 00:22:11.520
Next time:

00:22:12.620 --> 00:22:16.620
<i>"Si Si Ciao ~ On These Roman Roofs"</i>

00:22:25.230 --> 00:22:29.330
<i>Si Si Ciao, why do the good times</i>

00:22:29.430 --> 00:22:33.630
<i>seem to end so soon?</i>

00:22:33.830 --> 00:22:37.830
<i>Si Si Ciao, we're all friends</i>

00:22:38.030 --> 00:22:42.030
<i>Let's meet again on these Roman roofs</i>

00:22:42.640 --> 00:22:46.940
<i>Your laughing voice dances</i>

00:22:46.940 --> 00:22:50.840
<i>Once again in the sky</i>

00:22:51.240 --> 00:22:58.140
<i>Your pocket bursting with memories</i>

00:22:59.840 --> 00:23:03.740
<i>Si Si Ciao, goodbye but for now</i>

00:23:03.940 --> 00:23:07.940
<i>Let's meet again on these Roman roofs</i>
